15:13:16 waited {"status": "Built 6 parts, TransferCase_E4_Layout, TransferCase_E4_Carrier_Carrier and TransferCase_E4.SLDASM; no interference between the gears in any mode, where they stand. Its turning gears are mated to turn in each of its 4 modes, one configuration each (2H, 4H, N and 4L), and SolidWorks reports no mate in error in any of them: it opens in 2H; to switch mode, double-click another mode's configuration in SolidWorks' ConfigurationManager. Drag Sun in SolidWorks to turn one train and FrontDog to turn the other. RangeSlv and ModeSlv slide along Rear, each to its place in each mode. The 3 copies of Pl turn on Carrier, and TransferCase_E4_Carrier_Carrier holds Carrier's axes and planes only: a plate and pins are yours to add. Ring stays fixed where it is placed: its shaft does not turn. A turn you give the gears in one mode shows in every mode, so a dog can stand across its sleeve in another mode; to put the gears back there, press Update SolidWorks with that mode showing. 1 thing to do by hand: Assign a material to each of the 6 parts; the build leaves it unset."}
